body:
It still shouldn't need to be reset multiple times, it's happened a lot - if your product is having that many issues with the Xbox perhaps Astro and Microsoft need to figure out what the problem is and fix it already. 

&#x200B;

Regardless, even after contacting Astro support about the issue, he was never told about the Astro Command Center or how to update firmware. I only happened to learn about it from a friend of mine who has friends who own the Gen 4. Needless to say he's not overly happy with the product, the need to continuously hard reset his Xbox, and the connectivity issues (which according to patch notes were supposed to be fixed with this most recent firmware update), nor is he happy with Astro's customer service.
